" Installed by copying it to ~/.vim/vimrc.
" See settings/vim/README.md.

" Start from Vim's own defaults.vim, which Vim stops loading as soon as any vimrc exists. macOS's
" /usr/bin/vim also switches it off in its system vimrc, hence the unlet. Vims older than 8.0, and
" some minimal builds, have no defaults.vim, and sourcing a missing file stops every startup with
" an error.
unlet! skip_defaults_vim
if filereadable(expand('$VIMRUNTIME/defaults.vim'))
  source $VIMRUNTIME/defaults.vim
endif

" defaults.vim only turns the mouse on in every mode when $TERM contains "xterm". Anywhere else,
" such as tmux or screen, it leaves out the command line (mouse=nvi), and without defaults.vim
" there's no mouse at all. Not redundant, so keep it.
set mouse=a

" Vim only picks the SGR mouse protocol by itself for terminals it recognises, and tmux isn't one,
" so there clicks past column 223 go astray. tmux understands SGR, so ask for it.
if has('mouse_sgr') && &term =~ '^\(tmux\|screen\)'
  set ttymouse=sgr
endif

" The Terminal.app profiles are dark, and Vim picks colours that read on a light background unless
" told otherwise.
set background=dark
